 src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1605759953i/55939473.jpg" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://dryofg8nmyqjw.cloudfront.net/images/no-cover.png';"/> The Data Vault Guru: a pragmatic guide on building a data vault Patrick Cuba 5.00 6   ratings 1   review Want to Read Rate this book The data vault methodology presents a unique opportunity to model the enterprise data warehouse using the same automation principles applicable in today’s software delivery, continuous integration, continuous delivery and continuous deployment while still maintaining the standards expected for governing a corporation’s most valuable data. This book provides at first the landscape of a modern architecture and then as a thorough guide on how to deliver a data model that flexes as the enterprise flexes, the data vault. Whether the data is structured, semi-structured or even unstructured one thing is clear, there is always a model either applied early (schema-on-write) or applied late (schema-on-read). Today’s focus on data governance requires that we know what we retain about our customers, the data vault provides that focus by delivering a methodology focused on all aspects about the customer and provides some of the best practices for modern day data compliance. The book will delve into every data vault modelling artefact, its automation with sample code, raw vault, business vault, testing framework, a build framework, sample data vault models, how to build automation patterns on top of a data vault and even offer an extension of data vault that provides automated timeline correction, not to mention variation of data vault designed to provide audit trails, metadata control and integration with agile delivery tools. 1170 pages, Kindle Edition Published October 6, 2020 Book details &amp; editions Loading... Loading... About the author Patrick Cuba 2   books Follow Follow Ratings &amp; Reviews What do you think? Rate this book Write a Review Friends &amp; Following Create a free account to discover what your friends think of this book! Community Reviews 5.00 6   ratings 1   review 5 stars 6 (100%) 4 stars 0 (0%) 3 stars 0 (0%) 2 stars 0 (0%) 1 star 0 (0%) Search review text Filters Displaying 1 of 1 review Simon 1 review Follow Follow July 13, 2026 Trying to read up on DV these days is a little like studying theology. This book is the "Letters From St Patrick", hints at the original dynamism of the idea in its youth, before it ossified into being a stagnant orthodoxy. The book is likely of interest to people who study the history of data methods. If you are having to read up because your organisation has "just discovered" DV, then check the dates and be clear-eyed that this 2020 book has "pragmatic" in the title, as the current "ivory towers" version was on the march. There are many interesting ideas and concepts in DV that serve as useful tools to add to the mental toolbox. I would love to bump into Patrick Cuba someday and discuss the earlier versions of DV with him. Sadly, these days, it is best to avoid anyone who is wildly enthusiastic about the topic. You will notice a fanatical zeal in their eyes. They may also start to dribble from the corners of their mouths when they list off layers upon layers of bolt-on complexity from memory. That is the hallmark of the official Cargo Cult DV2. As long as you read between the lines and take it with a "Big O" pinch of salt (pun intended), you will be fine. If someone is trying to convince you that DV is a "hot" new idea, then be aware that this book marked the point where it entered into its geriatric years. If you are wondering why I gave 5 stars yet do not sound that thrilled about DV both can be true at the same time. I have seen the bolt-on Frankenstein complexity of DV "In Action" on a new project. It was a brownfield project in all senses of the word. Yet if you must read a book about DV2, then this is the must-read book. Hence, 5 stars. Like Comment Displaying 1 of 1 review Join the discussion Add a quote Start a discussion Ask a question Company About us Careers Terms Privacy Interest Based Ads Ad Preferences Your Ads Privacy Choices Help Work With Us Authors Advertise Authors &amp; ads blog Connect © 2026 Goodreads LLC {"props":{"pageProps":{"apolloState":{"ROOT_QUERY":{"__typename":"Query","getAdsTargeting({\"getAdsTargetingInput\":{\"contextual\":{}}})":{"__typename":"AdsTargeting","behavioral":null,"contextual":null},"getSiteHeaderBanner":{"__typename":"SiteHeaderBanner","altText":"A Decade of Hit Books","clickthroughUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/blog/show/3184?ref=DecadeHits26_eb","desktop1xPhoto":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/siteheaderbannerimages/1787763604i/761.jpg","desktop2xPhoto":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/siteheaderbannerimages/1787763611i/762.jpg","mobile1xPhoto":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/siteheaderbannerimages/1787763617i/763.jpg","mobile2xPhoto":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/siteheaderbannerimages/1787763622i/764.jpg","siteStripColor":"#FFAB59"},"getBookByLegacyId({\"legacyId\":\"55939473\"})":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.pxDFktfkbvGxZZir"},"getPageBanner({\"getPageBannerInput\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.pxDFktfkbvGxZZir\",\"pageName\":\"book_show\"}})":{"__typename":"PageBanner","type":null,"message":null},"getReviews":{"__typename":"BookReviewsConnection","totalCount":1,"edges":[{"__typename":"BookReviewsEdge","node":{"__ref":"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.PGoTEeDZnTZLsbIVekF9sA"}}],"pageInfo":{"__typename":"PageInfo","prevPageToken":"NjYsMTc4Mzk2NDg5Nzg0Mg","nextPageToken":""}},"getSocialSignals({\"bookId\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.pxDFktfkbvGxZZir\",\"shelfStatus\":[\"CURRENTLY_READING\",\"TO_READ\"]})":[{"__typename":"SocialSignal","name":"CURRENTLY_READING","count":